  "tagline": "The Leather City that kept its own schools: a district of five schools, a $62 million stadium, and Lake Lanier's dam at the edge of town.",
  "summary": "Buford began in 1872 as a stop on the railroad to Charlotte and grew around the Bona Allen tannery, which made saddles, collars and shoes until 1981. It is the one city in Gwinnett County with its own school district, and it spends on it: an $85 million high school in 2019, a $62 million stadium in 2025. Most of the city is in Gwinnett; a northern sliver is in Hall. Buford Dam and Lake Lanier are a quarter-hour away, the Mall of Georgia closer.",
